=== Legibility table (frozen catmus CER, n=300, GT=base letters) — spec §6.5.24/§6.5.30 20260823 ===
render type          stamps       raw      +gentle   +harsh
Real crop            real image   0.0479   --        --
synth anno-renders   no-stamps    0.0317   0.0338    0.0915
synth anno-renders   WITH stamps  0.1114   0.1225    0.1820
synth medical        no-stamps    0.0491   0.0528    0.1110
synth medical        WITH stamps  0.1506   0.1607    0.2133

Three separable legibility factors, ranked by damage:
  1. STAMPS      +0.08..0.10 CER (composited scribal glyphs frozen catmus can't map to base-letter GT) — biggest
  2. HARSH aug   +0.06..0.07
  3. GENTLE aug  +0.002..0.011 (negligible — legibility-preserving, the point of the gentle preset)
No-stamps clean renders read at/below real level (anno raw 0.0317 < real 0.0479). Stamped+harsh
medical 0.2133 reproduces original §6.5.24 "synth medical 0.2082". Caveat: frozen catmus never
trained on the stamps; a trained model learns the mappings.

--- Matched-lines note (2026-08-23) ---
The "Real crop" row above (0.0479) is the 300 VALIDATION crops — a DIFFERENT line set than the
synth anno-renders (which render the full_annotated/train lines). Matched reference: the real
full_annotated crops of the SAME 300 lines as the anno-renders = CER 0.0520 (≈ validation 0.0479,
≈ documented 0.0525). So same-text comparison holds: same 300 annotated lines read at 0.0520 as
REAL crops vs 0.0317 as clean no-stamps RENDERS (≈ real) vs 0.1114 stamped — the degradation is
the STAMPS, not the rendering (content held constant).
